    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Before another past",
     "texto": [
      "The **pluperfect** tells of something that had already happened **before another moment in the past**. It is formed with **haber** in the imperfect + a **participle**.\n\n- Cuando **llegué**, Ana ya **había salido**.\n\nAna left first; then I arrived. The older action goes in the pluperfect.\n\nIt is accompanied by words like **ya**, **todavía no**, **antes** and **nunca**. The participle **does not change** for gender or number."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Haber in the imperfect + participle",
     "texto": [
      "The forms of **haber** in the imperfect are:\n\n- yo **había** salido\n- tú **habías** salido\n- él, ella, usted **había** salido\n- nosotros **habíamos** salido\n- vosotros **habíais** salido\n- ellos, ellas, ustedes **habían** salido\n\nNegation and pronouns go **before** **haber**: **no** había visto, **nos** había esperado. Nothing comes between **haber** and the participle.\n\nCommon irregular participles: **hecho**, **dicho**, **escrito**, **visto**, **puesto**, **vuelto**, **abierto**, **roto**."
     ],
